{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Page counts are fixed. The problem was `num_pages` in `repo/paging.py`: it rounded down, so whenever the last page was only partly full, that page wasn't counted. 101 rows at 10 per page came out as 10 pages instead of 11.\n\nI changed it to round up instead:\n\n```4:12:repo/paging.py\ndef num_pages(total, per_page):\n    // ... docstring ...\n    if per_page <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"per_page must be positive\")\n    return -(-total // per_page)\n```\n\nBoth tests pass now. I also checked a few edge cases by hand:\n- **Zero rows:** 0 pages.\n- **1 to 10 rows:** 1 page.\n- **11 rows:** 2 pages.\n- **100 rows:** 10 pages.\n- **101 rows:** 11 pages.\n\nThis also fixes the two things that call `num_pages`: `page_summary` in `repo/rows.py` and the older `old_page_count` helper. For 101 rows, `page_summary` now reports 11 pages with the last page starting at row 100, where before it said the last page started at row 90.\n\nI didn't touch the other TODOs in the repo (the slow duplicate removal, the manual padding, adding caching) because they're separate from page counts."}]},"session_id":"2b04c011-e06c-49fd-8632-00a0ee60a4bb"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":31394,"duration_api_ms":31394,"is_error":false,"result":"I'll look through the workspace to find the export and pagination code.Found it: `num_pages` in `repo/paging.py` uses floor division, so any partial last page gets dropped. Switching it to ceiling division.Page counts are fixed. The problem was `num_pages` in `repo/paging.py`: it rounded down, so whenever the last page was only partly full, that page wasn't counted. 101 rows at 10 per page came out as 10 pages instead of 11.\n\nI changed it to round up instead:\n\n```4:12:repo/paging.py\ndef num_pages(total, per_page):\n    // ... docstring ...\n    if per_page <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"per_page must be positive\")\n    return -(-total // per_page)\n```\n\nBoth tests pass now. I also checked a few edge cases by hand:\n- **Zero rows:** 0 pages.\n- **1 to 10 rows:** 1 page.\n- **11 rows:** 2 pages.\n- **100 rows:** 10 pages.\n- **101 rows:** 11 pages.\n\nThis also fixes the two things that call `num_pages`: `page_summary` in `repo/rows.py` and the older `old_page_count` helper. For 101 rows, `page_summary` now reports 11 pages with the last page starting at row 100, where before it said the last page started at row 90.\n\nI didn't touch the other TODOs in the repo (the slow duplicate removal, the manual padding, adding caching) because they're separate from page counts.","session_id":"2b04c011-e06c-49fd-8632-00a0ee60a4bb","request_id":"43b777ff-237e-4274-ad11-b14b0fdd1c2b","usage":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":1591,"cacheReadTokens":84341,"cacheWriteTokens":17832}}
